hifiberry-shairport (1:5.2.1.5) stable; urgency=medium

  * Restore the AirPlay 1/2 choice, this time as a real setting. The old
    control in the web interface wrote to an in-memory object and called no
    API, so it never changed anything, and it stopped rendering at all when
    this package became an extension. Declare airplay_version as an ordinary
    select in the player descriptor, and have start-shairport read it from
    the config database, falling back to shairport-sync.conf when it is
    unset or config-server cannot be reached -- the script still has to work
    during an image build and on a device whose web interface never ran.
    Only "1" and "2" are accepted; any other stored value is treated as
    unset rather than silently selecting AirPlay 2.
    Applies the next time the player starts, like every other plugin
    setting.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:00:00 +0000

hifiberry-shairport (1:5.2.1.4) stable; urgency=medium

  * postinst: do not restart config-server. When the web interface installs
    an extension, config-server is the process running apt and it holds the
    install job the UI polls in memory, so restarting from the postinst --
    which runs during dpkg's configure step, mid-install -- destroyed that
    job. The package installed correctly (apt runs under systemd-run and
    survives) but the UI reported the install as lost. The restart was also
    unnecessary: configurator re-reads conf.d in place after every extension
    install.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 18:30:00 +0000

hifiberry-shairport (1:5.2.1.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Publish as a HiFiBerry extension: declare the XB-Extension metadata so
    the package appears in the web interface's extension catalog, and drop
    it from the hbos-full bundle. AirPlay is now installed on demand rather
    than shipped with every full image.
  * Ship the WebUI player descriptor and its icon
    (/etc/hifiberry/players.d/shairport.json). These were never packaged --
    dpkg -S found no owner for them on a running device -- so AirPlay
    appeared in the Players page only where someone had placed the files by
    hand. As an extension that gap would be fatal: installing it would
    register no player at all.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:30:00 +0000

hifiberry-shairport (1:5.2.1.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Ship the ACR player definition as /etc/audiocontrol/players.d/shairport.json.
    The definition used to live in audiocontrol.json, which meant the package
    that provides shairport-sync and the file that defines the player were
    owned by different packages.
  * postinst: stop writing the players.d drop-in at configure time now that
    it ships as a package conffile; dpkg owns it and preserves local edits
    across upgrades instead of it being silently overwritten every run.
  * postrm: only delete the players.d conffile on purge, not on plain remove,
    so local edits survive a remove/reinstall cycle.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 11:59:07 +0000

hifiberry-shairport (1:5.2.1.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Update Shairport Sync to upstream 5.2.1 (was 5.1). Notable for HiFiBerryOS:
    - Metadata: upstream restored the "classic" metadata feature bits
      (artwork/progress/text) as the default. 5.1 advertised only the new
      plist-based metadata (AirPlay feature bit 50), which audiocontrol's
      shairport listener (classic ssnc/core packets on UDP 5555) does not
      parse. Keep diagnostics.get_plist_metadata unset/"no".
    - Fixed a hang when an unfixable error occurs: the alsa backend mutex is
      now released, so shairport-sync exits and systemd can restart it instead
      of the unit hanging.
    - New exit handler for clean shutdown (normal, fatal-error and D-Bus/MPRIS
      quit paths).
    - 5.2.1 additionally drops an obsolete log_to_syslog() reference that broke
      --with-libdaemon builds (not used here).
  * The log_output_to setting and --log-to-syslog option are now obsolete
    upstream; neither is used by our config or start-shairport.
  * NQPTP stays at 1.2.6: shairport-sync 5.2.1 still requires shm structures
    version 10, so 1.2.7/1.2.8 (systemd unit path + man page only) add nothing
    for this package.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0000

hifiberry-shairport (1:5.1.0.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * postinst: generate a D-Bus own-policy for the media-player user from
    /etc/hifiberry.user (shairport-sync-hifiberry.conf) so shairport-sync can
    acquire its control interface (org.gnome.ShairportSync /
    org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.ShairportSync) on the system bus. The shipped policy
    only allowed root/shairport-sync, but on HiFiBerryOS shairport runs as the
    configured user, so audiocontrol can now DropSession/RemoteCommand to stop
    AirPlay when another player takes over.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 09 Jul 2026 10:30:00 +0000

hifiberry-shairport (1:5.1.0.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Adopt the upstream.patch version scheme: upstream shairport-sync is 5.1.0
    (3 digits) and the HiFiBerry packaging revision is the 4th digit. An epoch
    (1:) is used so this sorts above the previously-published 5.1.1/5.1.2, which
    are being unpublished.
  * Build with --with-metadata-multicast so shairport-sync emits AirPlay
    metadata to the UDP socket (socket_address/socket_port, 127.0.0.1:5555).
    Previously only --with-metadata was passed, which compiles in the metadata
    pipe but NOT the multicast/socket output, so audiocontrol (which listens on
    UDP 5555) never saw AirPlay play state. Fixes AirPlay not being detected /
    not participating in active-player switching.
  * Includes the earlier config-server restart in postinst (was 5.1.2).

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 09 Jul 2026 09:30:00 +0000

